# Build context exclusions.
#
# The production stage does `COPY . .`, so anything reachable here can be baked
# into an image that is later pushed to a registry. Secrets and host artefacts
# must not be reachable.

# Secrets and local environment. .env.example is deliberately NOT excluded:
# it is tracked, carries no secrets, and documents the runtime contract.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
auth.json

# Version control and CI. Every .gitignore is excluded at every depth: they are
# repository bookkeeping with no runtime role, and the image must not rely on
# the nested storage placeholders to create its directory tree. The production
# stage mkdir's that tree explicitly instead.
.git
.gitignore
**/.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github

# Host-installed dependencies. vendor/ is rebuilt inside the image from the
# committed lockfile; copying the host copy would defeat the pinned build.
vendor
node_modules

# Generated runtime data. The entrypoint recreates the directory tree.
storage/app/private/*
storage/app/public/*
storage/framework/cache/*
storage/framework/sessions/*
storage/framework/testing/*
storage/framework/views/*
storage/logs/*
bootstrap/cache/*

# Test and tooling caches
.phpunit.cache
.phpunit.result.cache
.phpactor.json

# Frontend build output
public/build
public/hot
public/storage

# Editor and OS metadata
.idea
.vscode
.cursor
.codex
.fleet
.nova
.zed
.history
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Documentation and project instructions: not needed at runtime and they make
# the context larger and the image layers noisier.
docs
*.md
!README.md

# Docker inputs themselves are consumed by explicit COPY, not by `COPY . .`
compose.yaml
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
